#subtitle: Issues of taxation and money printing.

= Fiscal Policy

Fiscal policy involves issues of taxation and funds.


@fiscal_menu

- @raise: Increase overall taxes.
- @cut: Cut overall taxes.
- @issue: Issue large sums of money.
- @root: Do not change the tax system.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@cut
subtitle: -2 funds, -1 every quarter
unavailable-subtitle: -2 funds - [? if upper_tax_rates < -5 or lower_tax_rates < -5 : Tax rates are already too low. ?]
choose-if: funds >= 2 and upper_tax_rates >= -5 and lower_tax_rates >= -5
on-arrival: funds -= 2; income -= 1; upper_tax_rates -= 1; lower_tax_rates -= 1; new_middle_kmt += 5*(1-dissent); old_middle_kmt += 4*(1-dissent); workers_kmt += 3*(1-dissent); unemployed -= 0.5; economic_growth += 0.6; inflation += 1;

Cutting taxes benefits most the rich and middle-class, who pay more taxes than the working class. Our coalition partners are happy at our orthodox economic course.

@raise
subtitle: +2 funds [? if centralize > 0 : (+1 for tax reforms) ?], +1 every quarter
unavailable-subtitle: Tax rates are already too high.
choose-if: upper_tax_rates <= 5 and lower_tax_rates <= 5
on-arrival: funds += 2; income += 1; funds += 1 if centralize > 0; new_middle_kmt -= 4; old_middle_kmt -= 4; workers_kmt -= 4; unemployed += 0.2; lower_tax_rates += 1; upper_tax_rates += 1; workers_kmt -= 5 if lower_tax_rates > 1; inflation -= 1.1; economic_growth -= 0.6; new_middle_kmt -= 2 if upper_tax_rates > 1; old_middle_kmt -= 2 if upper_tax_rates > 1;

Raising taxes hurts our support among all those who pay taxes. [? if in_grand_coalition or in_weimar_coalition : However, our coalition partners are more supportive of the idea of "shared sacrifice" than simply taxing the rich. ?] Increasing taxes also decreases economic demand, which may lead to more unemployment.

@issue
subtitle: +2 funds - this will considerably level up inflation.
unavailable-subtitle: Inflation is getting too high.
choose-if: inflation < 10
on-arrival: funds += 2; inflation += 3; new_middle_kmt -= 4; old_middle_kmt -= 4; workers_kmt -= 4; unemployed += 2; workers_kmt -= 5 if lower_tax_rates > 1; inflation -= 1.1; economic_growth -= 0.6; new_middle_kmt -= 2 if upper_tax_rates > 1; old_middle_kmt -= 2 if upper_tax_rates > 1;

Issuing more sums of cash will start taking a toll on our inflation.
